     "Room number five would be the room of feeling, because I feel like sometimes memories are not felt without are not fully understood without how they're felt, and it each part of the room would have like a different emotions that I lived with and in a sub categories too like not just excitement but like uh versions of excitement and not just melancholy, but acceptance and also admittance and all those different things.",
     "Room number six would be me through the years in terms of like all the times, all the versions of me that I became and it would have like me as a child, me as a teenager, me as a and the through line of this same unwavering will that I have of what I wanna become and who I am and it would show me the worlds that I built around me and the things that I've done. Room number six would be dedicated to the something not me.",
